{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "d8fe6b32-bc0a-8d2b-a1ca-bb74710b5a8d",
  "created_at": "2026-01-26T10:13:39-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Gina Grasso",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:09:18-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise, how can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:09:23-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, hi. Can you hear me okay? I've got wicked bad service in here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:09:30-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you, a little choppy but go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:09:35-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So I'm calling about plowing. I'm at 421 Chapel Street, up on the Hill. Plow came through, I don't know, sometime in the middle of the night, and then it turned to rain and now it's like a slushy wall at the end of my driveway. [line breaks up]"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:09:55-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You broke up on me there. You're at 421 Chapel, and there's a wall of slush at the end of the driveway?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:10:04-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, exactly. Well, a wall of heavy, wet, concrete-y snow. And honestly it's the same every time. We're on a dead end, so we get done last. Always. Like, everyone else on the Hill is clear by breakfast and we're the afterthought."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:10:21-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, dead ends do tend to be the last ones on the route. Did the plow go through at all this morning, or just overnight?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:10:31-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Overnight, I think, like before the rain really started. Then nothing since. And now it's ten o'clock Monday and it's all packed and heavy and I can't even get the car out. [inaudible] shovel it, but it's like lifting a sandbag."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:10:47-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. That slush gets awful once it's rained on. So what you're asking is for a plow to come back down Chapel and clean it up?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:10:59-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. Can somebody just come back down? Even one pass. I'm not asking for the red carpet."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:11:07-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I'll put in a request for a return pass on your street. I can't tell you the exact time, the crews are still working through the whole city after this one, and with the rain they're dealing with a lot of heavy stuff."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:11:25-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, no, I get that. I just, it's the dead end thing. We're always at the bottom of the list. It's like nobody remembers there's houses down here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:11:37-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me make sure I have the spot right. Is it the end of Chapel where it dead-ends, or is it partway down?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:11:47-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Partway down, but past the last cross street. So it's the dead end part, basically. Number 421. Sorry, the signal here is garbage, I'm standing by the front window. [line breaks up] Can you hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:12:02-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I got you. Past the last cross street, 421 Chapel. Got it. Anything blocking the plow, like cars parked on the street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:12:11-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, my neighbor's car is out, but it's pulled up pretty far. Speaking of my neighbor, she's out there right now with a shovel, and I'm just waiting for her to knock on the door asking for sugar. She borrows sugar so much it's become a whole joke. I told her just buy a bag."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:12:33-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, at least she's shoveling. Hopefully she's got her own sugar by the time the plow shows up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:12:41-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right? Anyway. So, you'll send somebody back?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:12:45-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm logging the request now with your address and a note that it's the dead-end stretch and it's packed with heavy slush. The supervisor will see it and route a truck as they can."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:12:59-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Is there a number if I need to call back? Or do I just call you again?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:13:07-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can call this line again. Do you want me to put a callback number on the request, in case the crew has a question?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:13:17-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. It's 401-555-0161."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:13:19-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0161. Got it. And it's Gina?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:13:22-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, Gina Grasso. G-R-A-S-S-O."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:13:24-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect, Gina. Thanks for calling. And be careful shoveling that stuff, it's heavy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:13:30-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Will do. Thanks, Denise. Hopefully I see a plow before lunch."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-26T10:13:35-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "We'll do what we can. Take care."
    }
  ],
